SIL6250 C interface, ABI version 0

Build with `make -C sil6250-ffi check`. Install to a writable prefix with
`make -C sil6250-ffi install PREFIX=/absolute/local/prefix`.
DESTDIR, LIBDIR, INCLUDEDIR, CARGO and CARGO_TARGET_DIR are supported.
The installed pkg-config name is sil6250-ffi; the SONAME is
libsil6250_ffi.so.0. The shared library exports C symbols only.

Pointers passed by a caller must reference live memory of the declared size.
Paths must be NUL-terminated UTF-8 strings. Input memory must be readable;
output memory must be writable and must not overlap input buffers or handles.
Each engine handle is exclusively owned and must be used by one thread at a
time. Free it exactly once with sil6250_engine_free. A null handle is accepted
by free. Arbitrary non-null invalid pointers cannot be validated by this API.

engine_new returns null on invalid configuration or device-open failure.
It requires fresh random PSK provisioning by default; setup and handshake
failures never fall back to public keys in this mode. SIL6250_PSK_MODE
accepts auto, provision, replay or legacy. Unknown or non-UTF-8 values fail
before opening the device. auto, replay and legacy are explicit compatibility
modes that permit public keys. The legacy fallback key remains shiba.
Provisioning does not authenticate the sensor against a hardware trust anchor:
the key blob is obfuscated and recoverable by an observer of the mailbox.

capture requires exactly SIL6250_IMAGE_SIZE bytes. Its return value is 1 for
a frame, 0 for a timeout and -1 for failure. wait_lift returns false on a
timeout or failure. Without an operation control, connection setup and mailbox operations can take
additional time beyond the capture timeout. engine_set_control installs a shared
time budget across connection setup, capture, retries and finger-lift polling.
It accepts a nonzero millisecond timeout and an optional cancellation callback.
The callback is called synchronously on the engine thread, must not block or
unwind, and returns nonzero to cancel. Its user_data must remain valid until
the control is replaced or the engine is freed. IRQ waits check cancellation
in intervals of at most 50 ms; operating-system scheduling is not a real-time
guarantee. Engine handles still require exclusive access.

frame_quality and frame_ncc return -1 for invalid input sizes. frame_extract
returns the number of bytes written, or -1 without writing if the output is
too small. frame_score returns the best gallery score, or -1 for invalid
input. gallery_valid reports whether the gallery encoding is accepted.
frame_matches accepts a threshold from 1 to 200 and returns 1 for a match,
0 for no match, or -1 for invalid input. It validates the whole gallery before
matching and stops after the first reference reaching the threshold. Added
in interface version 0.2.0; the earlier exports and ABI-0 SONAME are retained.

A gallery contains little-endian u32 lengths followed by serialized Features.
It must contain 1 to 64 entries and fit within 2 MiB. The caller owns all image
and gallery buffers. The bridge retains none of these buffers after return.

Interface version 0.3.0 adds engine_set_control and prepared matching handles.
gallery_new validates and owns a parsed copy of the complete enrollment; it
returns null for invalid data. probe_new extracts and owns one image's features.
probe_matches uses these immutable handles with the same threshold and decision
rules as frame_matches. Both handles can be reused within an operation; release
each exactly once with its matching free function. Free accepts null. Do not use
a handle after freeing it, free it concurrently with matching, or pass a handle
of a different type. No enrollment format or matching threshold is changed.

